    [Cherry-pick][releases/v0.32.0rc][Feature][GLM-5.3-Flash] Enable static kernel compilation for GLM-5.3-Flash (from #20209) (#20503)
    
    Cherry-pick of PR #20209 onto `releases/v0.32.0rc`.
    
    Original PR: #20209
    Original author: @bnbryan
    
    ---
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Three fixes that make static kernel compilation work for GLM-5.3-Flash,
    all behind `enable_static_kernel`:
    
    - **Decode shape range.** `_compute_decode_cudagraph_batch_sizes` used
    the raw `cudagraph_capture_sizes`, but the V2 uniform-decode routine
    rounds token counts up to a multiple of `uniform_decode_query_len` —
    with MTP5 a configured 56 is captured at 60, which was never compiled.
    The range now includes the rounded sizes (capped at
    `max_cudagraph_capture_size`), only when `use_v2_model_runner` and
    `cudagraph_mode.separate_routine()` hold.
    - **Cache key.** The shape range is baked into the serialized FX
    artifacts, so `static_kernel_batch_sizes` is now a `compute_hash` factor
    when static kernels are enabled. Unchanged when disabled.
    - **`PoolKeyIndexer` blacklist.** It marks three metadata inputs
    value-dependent while its tiling never reads them. Added to the
    incompatible-op list so it keeps its dynamic binary.
    
